# scenario 05.3: A pull request without increment folders is not blocked
# On main, increment 07 has two automated scenarios without tests. A pull
# request that changes only README.md and a code file, and one that
# changes only the design note of 07, belong to no increment: each passes
# and names 07 as waiting with two scenarios.
env GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=Agent GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=agent@example.com GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=Agent GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=agent@example.com
cd repo
exec git init -q -b main
exec git add -A
exec git commit -q -m base

# README.md and a code file.
exec git checkout -q -b docs-and-code main
cp ../readme README.md
cp ../edit internal/x.go
exec git commit -q -a -m change
exec factory check-tests --base main
stdout '^check-tests: waiting 07-later 2 scenarios without tests$'
stdout '^check-tests: ok \d+ checked$'
! stdout ': error '

# Only the design note of 07.
exec git checkout -q -b note-07 main
cp ../note-07 docs/increments/07-later/design.md
exec git commit -q -a -m note
exec factory check-tests --base main
stdout '^check-tests: waiting 07-later 2 scenarios without tests$'
stdout '^check-tests: ok \d+ checked$'
! stdout ': error '

-- readme --
# Sample, changed
-- edit --
package x // changed
-- note-07 --
# Increment 07: later

## Goal

- The later tool works, also for a new kind of thing.

## Out of scope

- Everything else.

## Existing tools

- None found; searched for later tools.

## Interface

- `later run`

## Rollout

- Off switch: none. Failure signal: the tool rejects a correct input.

## Evidence

- Approved scenarios: 07.1 and 07.2.

## Scenarios

- **scenario 07.1** (automated) **A later thing works.** Given a later thing, the tool accepts it.
- **scenario 07.2** (automated) **A second later thing works.** Given a second later thing, the tool accepts it.
-- repo/README.md --
# Sample
-- repo/internal/x.go --
package x
-- repo/docs/increments/06-sample/design.md --
